          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            For most people the Champion 201323 is the right 2,000-watt inverter: dual fuel, about 39 pounds, 1,850 running watts and a published 53 dBA rating, at a price that leaves room for a second unit later. Buy the Honda EU2200i if quiet and longevity are worth roughly double to you, and the Generac GP2500i if you need the extra running watts for a microwave.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Whichever you choose, size it to running watts, not the box, keep it 20 feet from the house, and start it once a month. A small generator that starts on the first pull is worth more than a big one with stale fuel in the carburetor.
          </p>
